cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this repository, please cite it."
title: "Hyperbolic Embeddings of ICD-10-CM and the Loss-Temperature Confound in Reconstruction MAP"
abstract: >-
  Code, data pipeline, and experiments for a study of hyperbolic embeddings of
  the 46,817-node ICD-10-CM diagnostic ontology. The central result is a
  measurement: a single training-objective temperature moves reconstruction MAP
  from 0.78 to 0.99 while distortion stays flat and out-of-training retrieval
  falls, so reconstruction MAP alone cannot support the cross-method comparisons
  the hyperbolic-embedding literature draws from it. Extends Sala et al. (2018).
